<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Al-Azhar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">begun 970</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as al-Azhar mosque</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Al-Azhar is a mosque in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> begun in 970 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>, soon after the founding of the city. It became a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> teaching and later, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni</a> rulers, one of the most important centres of Islamic learning in the world. It remains a major university and religious institution today.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/al-azhar.jpg" alt="Al-Azhar" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wildoo78 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mosqu%C3%A9e_Al-Azhar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
